/-! # Fibrewise regular germs cut a flat slice

Source: Stacks Project, More on Morphisms, Tag 06LI, `lemma-slice-given-elements`,
retaining the flatness and local finite presentation conclusions, including zero equations
(blueprint: lem-sfb-scheme-fibre-regular-slice-flat).
-/

@[expose] public section

set_option autoImplicit false

universe u

open CategoryTheory

namespace AlgebraicGeometry

/-- Germs forming a regular sequence in a scheme fibre extend to sections on an affine
neighbourhood whose common closed zero subscheme contains the point and is flat and
locally of finite presentation over the base. The closed subscheme is explicitly the
spectrum of the quotient by the ideal generated by these sections, embedded via the
canonical affine chart, so its scheme structure is fixed.

Source: Stacks Project, More on Morphisms, Tag 06LI, `lemma-slice-given-elements`,
with the regular-immersion and base-change regular-immersion assertions omitted.
(blueprint: lem-sfb-scheme-fibre-regular-slice-flat).

Proof (the seven steps of the DAG node):
1. Choose compatible affine charts using def-sbc-locally-finite-presentation. By
   lem-weil-pbc-affine-open-stalk-localization express the finitely many germs as
   fractions. Invert the product of their denominators using
   lem-weil-pbc-affine-open-section-vanishing-prime and def-weil-open-immersion.
   Each germ is now represented by a section. Localization preserves finite
   presentation by adjoining one inverse variable and one relation.
2. For zero equations, apply lem-sfb-relative-flat-affine-charts to the restricted
   morphism and the identity of the base (locally of finite type by the empty
   generating set, def-weil-finite-type-morphism). Shrink inside the resulting flat
   locus to a basic affine open by lem-weil-pbc-spec-localization-away-basic-open.
   Its zero ideal defines the whole open, flat and locally of finite presentation.
3. For r = k + 1, the prefix is regular by def-weil-pbc-regular-sequence: every
   prefix quotient surjects onto the nonzero final quotient. All the germs lie in
   the maximal ideal, since a unit would make that final quotient zero. Apply the
   induction hypothesis to obtain the flat, locally finitely presented prefix slice.
4. By def-pc-scheme-fibre, lem-weil-pbc-fibre-product-affine-spectra and
   lem-weil-pbc-affine-open-stalk-localization, its fibre stalk is the original fibre
   stalk modulo the prefix. The explicit tensor-product quotient and localization
   maps preserve the last germ; def-weil-closed-immersion identifies the slice.
5. The last germ on this prefix slice lies in the maximal ideal (the closed-immersion
   stalk map is local, def-pc-scheme) and is regular in its fibre stalk. Apply
   lem-trf-fibre-regular-element-flat-hypersurface to cut a flat, locally finitely
   presented hypersurface on an affine open of the prefix slice.
6. The new defining section and the image of the original last section have equal
   germs, so agree near the point (def-weil-pbc-module-stalk). Choose a basic open
   there and lift its defining function from the prefix quotient to the ambient
   affine ring, using lem-weil-pbc-spec-localization-away-basic-open and
   lem-weil-pbc-affine-open-section-vanishing-prime. The resulting ambient basic open
   is affine, and its closed subscheme cut out by all r equations is exactly the
   restriction of the hypersurface from Step 5, by the explicit quotient ring maps.
7. This restriction is flat by def-weil-flat-morphism, since open restriction
   preserves stalk maps. It is locally of finite presentation by the localization
   presentation of Step 1 and def-sbc-locally-finite-presentation. All section germs
   remain the specified ones, and the point belongs to the slice. This proves the
   induction step and hence the result for every r.
-/
theorem exists_affine_flat_slice_of_fiber_regular_sequence
    {T B : Scheme.{u}} (g : T ⟶ B) [LocallyOfFinitePresentation g]
    (t : T) (hflat : (g.stalkMap t).hom.Flat)
    (r : ℕ) (h : Fin r → T.presheaf.stalk t)
    (hregular : RingTheory.Sequence.IsRegular
      ((g.fiber (g t)).presheaf.stalk (g.asFiber t))
      (List.ofFn (fun i : Fin r ↦ (g.fiberStalkMap t).hom (h i)))) :
    ∃ (W : T.Opens) (hW : IsAffineOpen W) (ht : t ∈ W) (a : Fin r → Γ(T, W)),
      (∀ i : Fin r, T.presheaf.germ W t ht (a i) = h i) ∧
      t ∈ Set.range
        (Spec.map (CommRingCat.ofHom (Ideal.Quotient.mk (Ideal.span (Set.range a)))) ≫
          hW.fromSpec) ∧
      Flat
        (Spec.map (CommRingCat.ofHom (Ideal.Quotient.mk (Ideal.span (Set.range a)))) ≫
          hW.fromSpec ≫ g) ∧
      LocallyOfFinitePresentation
        (Spec.map (CommRingCat.ofHom (Ideal.Quotient.mk (Ideal.span (Set.range a)))) ≫
          hW.fromSpec ≫ g) := by
  sorry

end AlgebraicGeometry
